WEBVTT

00:00:10.330 --> 00:00:12.010
-(ROARS)
-(GASPS)

00:00:14.450 --> 00:00:15.730
(ROARS)

00:00:16.690 --> 00:00:17.690
You look funny.

00:00:20.250 --> 00:00:21.250
What?

00:00:25.050 --> 00:00:26.170
(GIRL YAWNING)

00:00:26.250 --> 00:00:28.250
GIRL 1: I'm so tired. What's going on?

00:00:28.530 --> 00:00:29.530
GIRL 2: It's the middle of the night.

00:00:30.290 --> 00:00:31.770
GIRL 3: A little funny green guy.

00:00:31.890 --> 00:00:32.930
(WHIMPERING)

00:00:37.250 --> 00:00:38.250
(ROARS)

00:00:38.770 --> 00:00:40.090
-(ROARS)
-(GASPS)

00:00:40.370 --> 00:00:42.210
(GIRLS CHATTERING INDISTINCTLY)

00:00:44.130 --> 00:00:46.810
GIRL 4: I want to touch it! It's so cute!

00:00:48.170 --> 00:00:50.330
-(PANTING)
-(STUDENTS MURMURING)

00:00:50.410 --> 00:00:51.490
James!

00:00:53.770 --> 00:00:56.730
No one goes near that door
until the authorities arrive.

00:00:56.970 --> 00:00:58.050
You don't think that could be...

00:00:58.170 --> 00:01:00.250
-It's Mike.
-But he could die out there!

00:01:02.730 --> 00:01:04.890
James, wait! We can help.

00:01:05.330 --> 00:01:08.490
Leave it to the old master of sales.

00:01:09.330 --> 00:01:10.530
We got a call in,
but that's the best we can do.

00:01:10.610 --> 00:01:11.610
Ahem!

00:01:11.850 --> 00:01:15.210
Don Carlton, sales.
Folks, today is your lucky day.

00:01:15.290 --> 00:01:18.210
How many times have you asked
yourself the following question...

00:01:18.290 --> 00:01:19.730
-Arrest him.
-Pardon?

00:01:19.810 --> 00:01:20.850
-(GRUNTS)
-(GROANS)

00:01:20.930 --> 00:01:21.930
Spread them, pops!

00:01:22.130 --> 00:01:23.650
-DON: Do you mind?
-Don't move!

00:01:23.770 --> 00:01:24.770
What? Sullivan!

00:01:25.130 --> 00:01:26.210
(GASPS) Don't you dare!

00:01:26.930 --> 00:01:28.210
Sullivan! Don't go in there!

00:01:30.610 --> 00:01:31.650
(GASPS)

00:01:35.930 --> 00:01:36.970
Mike?

00:01:37.970 --> 00:01:39.730
-Mike! (GASPS)
-(SIREN WAILS)

00:01:39.810 --> 00:01:41.890
WOMAN: The kids said
they saw something in the cabin.

00:01:41.970 --> 00:01:44.210
-They're calling it an alien.
-GIRL: It was!

00:01:44.530 --> 00:01:45.650
I saw a little green guy!

00:01:45.850 --> 00:01:47.130
What's the problem, ma'am?

00:01:47.530 --> 00:01:49.450
-(GASPS)
-(WIND WHOOSHING)

00:01:51.330 --> 00:01:52.770
(BREATHING HEAVILY)

00:01:54.810 --> 00:01:55.850
(WHISPERS) Mike?

00:01:56.050 --> 00:01:57.130
(GRUNTS)

00:01:57.650 --> 00:01:59.170
-(CROWD GASP)
-(GASPS)

00:01:59.450 --> 00:02:00.890
MALE CAMP COUNSELOR:
Bear! A bear in the camp!

00:02:02.530 --> 00:02:03.610
(PANTING)

00:02:03.730 --> 00:02:05.290
(GASPS LOUDLY)

00:02:10.290 --> 00:02:12.570
RANGER 2: Down this way. All right?

00:02:14.810 --> 00:02:16.610
(RANGERS CHATTERING
INDISTINCTLY)

00:02:17.610 --> 00:02:19.290
I heard something over here!

00:02:19.370 --> 00:02:20.650
-(SPLASH)
-(GASPS)

00:02:22.490 --> 00:02:23.890
(SIGHS) Mike!

00:02:25.810 --> 00:02:27.490
Come on, buddy.
Let's get you out of here.

00:02:33.650 --> 00:02:36.530
This is all my fault. I'm sorry.

00:02:38.650 --> 00:02:41.810
You were right.
They weren't scared of me.

00:02:44.690 --> 00:02:46.570
I did everything right.

00:02:46.730 --> 00:02:48.730
I wanted it more than anyone.

00:02:50.330 --> 00:02:53.530
And I thought...
I thought if I wanted it enough,

00:02:53.610 --> 00:02:55.370
I could show everybody that...

00:02:56.530 --> 00:02:59.010
That Mike Wazowski
is something special.

00:03:01.530 --> 00:03:02.930
And I'm just

00:03:04.770 --> 00:03:05.850
not.

00:03:12.250 --> 00:03:14.250
Look, Mike, I know how you feel.

00:03:14.530 --> 00:03:16.330
Don't do that! Please, don't do that!

00:03:16.410 --> 00:03:18.970
-You do not know how I feel.
-Mike, calm down.

00:03:19.210 --> 00:03:21.530
Monsters like you have everything.
You don't have to be good.

00:03:21.610 --> 00:03:23.890
You can mess up over and over again

00:03:23.970 --> 00:03:25.490
-and the whole world loves you.
-Mike...

00:03:25.610 --> 00:03:26.970
You'll never know what it's like to fail

00:03:27.050 --> 00:03:29.130
because you were born a Sullivan!

00:03:29.370 --> 00:03:30.330
Yeah, I'm a Sullivan.

00:03:30.410 --> 00:03:32.290
I'm the Sullivan who flunked every test.

00:03:32.370 --> 00:03:33.690
The one who got kicked out
of the program,

00:03:34.050 --> 00:03:36.210
the one who was so afraid
to let everyone down

00:03:36.290 --> 00:03:37.570
that I cheated.

00:03:37.890 --> 00:03:39.050
And I lied.

00:03:40.890 --> 00:03:42.250
(SIGHS)

00:03:42.730 --> 00:03:44.890
Mike, I'll never know how you feel,

00:03:46.570 --> 00:03:48.570
but you're not the only failure here.

00:03:52.730 --> 00:03:57.290
I act scary, Mike, but most of the time

00:03:58.810 --> 00:04:00.250
I'm terrified.

00:04:12.610 --> 00:04:14.490
How come you never
told me that before?

00:04:16.410 --> 00:04:17.530
Because

00:04:18.850 --> 00:04:20.850
we weren't friends before.

00:04:25.970 --> 00:04:27.050
-RANGER 3: Check the lake!
-(GASPS)

00:04:27.370 --> 00:04:29.570
-RANGER 4: I heard something here!
-(GASPS)

00:04:30.010 --> 00:04:31.570
-(GASPS)
-RANGER 5: This way!

00:04:32.010 --> 00:04:33.130
(PANTING)

00:04:35.370 --> 00:04:36.730
(RANGERS SHOUTING)

00:04:37.450 --> 00:04:38.890
RANGER 6: I saw movement!

00:04:39.330 --> 00:04:40.450
Over there!

00:04:44.450 --> 00:04:45.970
(PANTING)

00:04:46.050 --> 00:04:48.050
(GRUNTING)

00:04:50.650 --> 00:04:51.890
(SHOUTING CONTINUES)

00:04:53.130 --> 00:04:54.170
(GRUNTS)

00:04:56.090 --> 00:04:57.130
MIKE: Sulley!

00:04:59.650 --> 00:05:00.890
(PANTING IN RELIEF)

00:05:01.490 --> 00:05:03.130
(SHOUTING CONTINUES)

00:05:04.010 --> 00:05:05.130
RANGER 5: He's cornered!

00:05:10.690 --> 00:05:11.690
(BOTH GASP)

00:05:13.250 --> 00:05:14.490
No!

00:05:16.370 --> 00:05:17.370
They're still in there!

00:05:17.570 --> 00:05:20.370
Until the authorities arrive,
this door stays off!

00:05:20.650 --> 00:05:23.090
No! You can't do that! No!

00:05:23.410 --> 00:05:26.850
Enough! I want this room cleared now!

00:05:27.170 --> 00:05:28.490
-You can't do this!
-(ALL CLAMORING)

00:05:34.010 --> 00:05:35.330
-(GASPS)
-(SIREN WAILS)

00:05:40.170 --> 00:05:41.530
We got to get out of here!

00:05:43.410 --> 00:05:45.170
-Let them come.
-What?

00:05:45.410 --> 00:05:47.290
If we scare them,
I mean really scare them,

00:05:47.370 --> 00:05:50.170
we could generate enough scream
to power the door from this side!

00:05:50.530 --> 00:05:51.490
What are you talking about?

00:05:51.570 --> 00:05:53.290
I have read every book
about Scaring ever written.

00:05:53.370 --> 00:05:54.370
This could work!

00:05:54.530 --> 00:05:56.010
They're adults. I can't do this.

00:05:56.250 --> 00:05:57.690
Yes, you can. Just follow my lead.

00:06:01.210 --> 00:06:02.210
(DOOR CREAKING)

